      "editorial": {
        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "The point is not a generic Chicago tribute. Danny Seraphine is the original drummer who helped define the band's early rhythmic identity, and CTA rebuilds that horn-heavy jazz-rock language from inside the lineage rather than from outside it. Billboard's club scale should make the drum-horn architecture far more visible than it would be in an arena nostalgia package, and the first Japan appearance in eight years gives the Tokyo date a concrete reason to matter.",
          "trip_verdict": "Actively make room for one of the two Roppongi sets if early Chicago, drumming, horn arranging or the jazz-rock lineage is part of the Tokyo thread. It is strong enough to build the evening around without forcing the rest of a Kanto itinerary to bend around a touring project.",
