        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "This works because the arrangement changes the physical center of THE BAWDIES' music. ROY's voice normally rides a hard rhythm-and-blues engine; here the weight shifts to bow attack, voicing, counterline and piano under a singer whose phrasing still depends on groove. NAOTO's quartet is not decorative backing but the mechanism that has made ROCKIN' QUARTET a recurring reinterpretation series, and this chapter gives it a vocalist with enough rhythmic personality to make the collision meaningful.",
